window.DOCS["6ad7132045af13551e4861f5"]={"id":"6ad7132045af13551e4861f5","summary":{"title_zh":"議程項目 18(c) 非正式文件：海洋、沿岸及島嶼生物多樣性之科學與技術議題","what":"這是第二工作小組提出的非正式文件，內容為擬議決議文本，主題是海洋、沿岸與島嶼生物多樣性。文件涉及具生態或生物重要性海域的描述、同儕審查參考要素、國家管轄範圍以外海域的工作，以及相關科學指南與能力建構。","points":["決定延長「具生態或生物重要性海洋區域非正式諮詢小組」的任期，至第十八次締約方大會為止。","鼓勵締約方，並邀請其他政府、原住民族與地方社區、婦女、青年及利害關係人，共同參與具生態或生物重要性海域的描述與更新工作。","鼓勵締約方，並邀請其他政府，強化開發中國家（特別是低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）的科學與技術能力，並動員資源。","請執行秘書在資源許可下，協助各方發展海域描述的提交文件，並召開全球專家工作坊以彙整科學知識（工作坊的知識來源描述仍在方括號內）。","請執行秘書加強與聯合國海洋事務與海洋法司等機構的合作，並開發以環境 DNA、遙測等新技術監測海洋生物多樣性的科學指南。","歡迎（或注意到）《國家管轄範圍以外海域生物多樣性協定》於 2026 年 1 月 17 日生效，並鼓勵締約方加強區域海洋公約與區域漁業機構之間的協調與合作。"],"open":["第 2 段：是「歡迎」或「注意到」與具生態或生物重要性海域描述相關的提交文件。","第 6 段與附件一：是否採納同儕審查的「自願參考要素」或「自願指南」（英文以方括號並列兩種名稱），以及是否加入其他相容的科學標準。","第 9(b)–(c) 段：全球專家工作坊要彙整的知識來源寫法，以及是否與國家管轄範圍以外海域協定的秘書處合作、是否編撰相關資訊報告。","第 10、13 段與第 16–17 段：是否歡迎協定生效、是否鼓勵其他機構採用公約工具，以及是否設立國家管轄範圍以外海域工作之非正式諮詢小組（附件二）。","第 12 段與第 14 段：利害關係人參與的措辭（是否列入原住民族與地方社區、婦女與青年），以及海洋保護區未達第 3 目標品質要素的描述。","第 18(b) 段：是否更新三份文件（海洋保護區選址科學指南、寒冷水域生物多樣性自願工作計畫、海洋與沿岸環評指南）。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p001.md","en":[{"t":"Agenda item 18 (c)"},{"t":"Other scientific and technical issues related to the"},{"t":"implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global"},{"t":"Biodiversity Framework: marine and coastal"},{"t":"biodiversity and island biodiversity"},{"t":"Working Group II"},{"t":"Marine and coastal biodiversity and island biodiversity"},{"t":"Non-paper"},{"t":"The Conference of the Parties,"},{"t":"Reaffirming Articles 3, 4, 5 and 22 of the Convention on Biological Diversity,1 as well as its decisions VIII/24 of 31 March 2006, IX/20 of 30 May 2008, X/29 of 29 October 2010, XI/17 of"},{"t":"19 October 2012, XII/22 of 17 October 2014, XIII/12 of 17 December 2016, in particular its paragraph 3, 14/9 of 29 November 2018, 15/24 and 15/26 of 19 December 2022, 16/16 of 30 October 2024 and 16/17 of 1 November 2024,"},{"t":"Recalling resolution 80/110 of 9 December 2025 of the General Assembly of the United Nations on oceans and the law of the sea, including its preambular paragraphs on the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea,2,3,4"},{"t":"Recognizing that the modification of descriptions of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and the description of new areas is an important scientific and technical process that contributes to the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework5 [and the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction],6"},{"t":"I"},{"t":"Ecologically or biologically significant marine areas"},{"t":"1. Decides to extend the term of the Informal Advisory Group on Ecologically or Biologically Significant Marine Areas until the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"2. [Welcomes][Takes note of] the submissions related to the description of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and the modification of existing descriptions, as contained in document CBD/SBSTTA/28/INF/2/Rev.1 and summarized in document CBD/SBSTTA/28/7/Add.1;"},{"t":"3. Encourages Parties, and invites other Governments, relevant organizations, indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and other stakeholders, to contribute to the work conducted under the Convention on Biological Diversity on ecologically or biologically significant marine areas, as appropriate and in accordance with decision 16/16, in order to improve the coverage of such areas around the world and ensure that the descriptions of those areas are kept up to date, recognizing the underrepresentation of areas beyond national jurisdiction in such descriptions;"},{"t":"4. Also encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations, to strengthen the scientific and technical capacities of developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States among them, including through the"},{"t":"1 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"2 Ibid., vol. 1833, No. 31363."},{"t":"3 Colombia reaffirms that the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea is not the only legal instrument governing activities"},{"t":"carried out in the oceans and seas. The participation of Colombia in the discussions under agenda item18 (c) of the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity does not affect its status or rights, nor can it be interpreted as a tacit or express acceptance of the provisions of the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea."},{"t":"4 Türkiye dissociates itself from the reference made to the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, to which it is not a Party. The participation of Türkiye in the discussions under agenda item 18 (c) of the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties cannot be construed as a change in the well-known legal position of Türkiye with regard to said instrument."},{"t":"5 Decision 15/4, annex."},{"t":"6 A/CONF.232/2023/4."}],"blocks":[{"md":"議程項目 18 (c)\n與實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要相關之其他科學與技術議題：海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性\n第二工作小組","html":"<p>議程項目 18 (c)<br />\n與實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要相關之其他科學與技術議題：海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性<br />\n第二工作小組</p>","en":[0,1,2,3,4]},{"md":"海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性\n非正式文件","html":"<p>海洋與沿岸生物多樣性及島嶼生物多樣性<br />\n非正式文件</p>","en":[5,6,7]},{"md":"締約方大會，","html":"<p>締約方大會，</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"**重申**《生物多樣性公約》第 3、4、5 及 22 條，¹ 以及其 2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之 IX/20、2010 年 10 月 29 日之 X/29、2012 年 10 月 19 日之 XI/17、2014 年 10 月 17 日之 XII/22、2016 年 12 月 17 日之 XIII/12（特別是其第 3 段）、2018 年 11 月 29 日之 14/9、2022 年 12 月 19 日之 15/24 與 15/26、2024 年 10 月 30 日之 16/16 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之 16/17，","html":"<p><strong>重申</strong>《生物多樣性公約》第 3、4、5 及 22 條，¹ 以及其 2006 年 3 月 31 日之決議 VIII/24、2008 年 5 月 30 日之 IX/20、2010 年 10 月 29 日之 X/29、2012 年 10 月 19 日之 XI/17、2014 年 10 月 17 日之 XII/22、2016 年 12 月 17 日之 XIII/12（特別是其第 3 段）、2018 年 11 月 29 日之 14/9、2022 年 12 月 19 日之 15/24 與 15/26、2024 年 10 月 30 日之 16/16 以及 2024 年 11 月 1 日之 16/17，</p>","en":[9,10]},{"md":"**回顧**聯合國大會 2025 年 12 月 9 日關於海洋與海洋法之決議 80/110，包括其關於《聯合國海洋法公約》之序言段落，²,³,⁴","html":"<p><strong>回顧</strong>聯合國大會 2025 年 12 月 9 日關於海洋與海洋法之決議 80/110，包括其關於《聯合國海洋法公約》之序言段落，²,³,⁴</p>","en":[11]},{"md":"**認識到**修改生態或生物重要海洋區域之描述以及描述新區域，是一項重要的科學與技術程序，有助於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要⁵ [以及《聯合國海洋法框架下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定》]，⁶","html":"<p><strong>認識到</strong>修改生態或生物重要海洋區域之描述以及描述新區域，是一項重要的科學與技術程序，有助於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要⁵ [以及《聯合國海洋法框架下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定》]，⁶</p>","en":[12,13,14]},{"md":"I\n生態或生物重要海洋區域","html":"<p>I<br />\n生態或生物重要海洋區域</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"1. **決定**將「生態或生物重要海洋區域非正式諮詢小組」之任期延長至第十八次締約方大會；","html":"<p>1. <strong>決定</strong>將「生態或生物重要海洋區域非正式諮詢小組」之任期延長至第十八次締約方大會；</p>","en":[15]},{"md":"2. [**歡迎**][**注意到**] 與生態或生物重要海洋區域之描述及現有描述之修改相關之提交內容，如文件 CBD/SBSTTA/28/INF/2/Rev.1 所載及文件 CBD/SBSTTA/28/7/Add.1 之摘要；","html":"<p>2. [<strong>歡迎</strong>][<strong>注意到</strong>] 與生態或生物重要海洋區域之描述及現有描述之修改相關之提交內容，如文件 CBD/SBSTTA/28/INF/2/Rev.1 所載及文件 CBD/SBSTTA/28/7/Add.1 之摘要；</p>","en":[16]},{"md":"3. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人，在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16，為在《生物多樣性公約》架構下進行之生態或生物重要海洋區域工作做出貢獻，以提高全球此類區域之覆蓋範圍，並確保該等區域之描述保持最新，同時認識到此類描述中對國家管轄範圍以外區域之代表性不足；","html":"<p>3. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府、相關組織、原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人，在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16，為在《生物多樣性公約》架構下進行之生態或生物重要海洋區域工作做出貢獻，以提高全球此類區域之覆蓋範圍，並確保該等區域之描述保持最新，同時認識到此類描述中對國家管轄範圍以外區域之代表性不足；</p>","en":[17,18]},{"md":"4. 亦**鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府及相關組織，透過包括","html":"<p>4. 亦<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府及相關組織，透過包括</p>","en":[19,20]},{"md":"---\n¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n² 同上，第 1833 卷，第 31363 號。\n³ 哥倫比亞重申，《聯合國海洋法公約》並非規範海洋與海域活動之唯一法律文書。哥倫比亞參與生物多樣性公約第十七次締約方大會議程項目 18 (c) 之討論，並不影響其地位或權利，亦不得被解釋為對《聯合國海洋法公約》條款之默示或明示接受。\n⁴ 土耳其與提及《聯合國海洋法公約》之處表示不一致，其並非該公約之締約方。土耳其參與締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 18 (c) 之討論，不得被解釋為土耳其對該文書之既定法律立場發生改變。\n⁵ 決議 15/4，附件。\n⁶ A/CONF.232/2023/4。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n² 同上，第 1833 卷，第 31363 號。<br />\n³ 哥倫比亞重申，《聯合國海洋法公約》並非規範海洋與海域活動之唯一法律文書。哥倫比亞參與生物多樣性公約第十七次締約方大會議程項目 18 (c) 之討論，並不影響其地位或權利，亦不得被解釋為對《聯合國海洋法公約》條款之默示或明示接受。<br />\n⁴ 土耳其與提及《聯合國海洋法公約》之處表示不一致，其並非該公約之締約方。土耳其參與締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 18 (c) 之討論，不得被解釋為土耳其對該文書之既定法律立場發生改變。<br />\n⁵ 決議 15/4，附件。<br />\n⁶ A/CONF.232/2023/4。</p>","en":[21,22,23,24,25]}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p002.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"mobilization of resources, to contribute to the work on ecologically or biologically significant marine areas under the Convention, as appropriate and in accordance with decision 16/16;"},{"t":"5. Further encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations, as appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances, to make use of the best available scientific information and compatible tools, taking into consideration the identification and recognition of essential and particularly sensitive habitats of marine species, in order to support the description and identification of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and inform ecosystem-based approaches and area-based conservation measures, including the designation and management of marine and coastal protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures, as appropriate, in support of Target 3 of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, while respecting the mandates of relevant international instruments and processes; [6. Adopts the voluntary [reference elements for good practice][guidelines] on peer-review processes for the description of areas meeting the criteria for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas [and other relevant compatible and complementary scientific criteria], as contained in annex I to the present decision, and invites Parties, other Governments and competent intergovernmental organizations to make use of them, as appropriate and in accordance with national circumstances and the respective mandates and procedures of competent intergovernmental organizations, without affecting or modifying the peer-review or decision-making processes established under other processes and noting that the voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] do not prejudice the sovereignty, sovereign rights or jurisdiction of States;]"},{"t":"7. Requests the Executive Secretary to continue to facilitate the work of the Informal Advisory Group on Ecologically or Biologically Significant Marine Areas in line with its terms of reference7 and to make a report on that work available at a meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"8. Also requests the Executive Secretary to include the submissions referred to in paragraph 2 above in the repository for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and to transmit them to the General Assembly of the United Nations, with a view to informing work under its relevant processes, as well as Parties, other Governments and relevant international organizations;"},{"t":"9. Further requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:"},{"t":"(a) To continue to facilitate and support efforts, as appropriate, including in collaboration with the regional and subregional technical and scientific cooperation support centres, to develop submissions for the modification of descriptions of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and the description of new areas, including through outreach, technical support and capacitybuilding;"},{"t":"(b) To convene a global expert workshop, with balanced regional representation, to collate, synthesize and review the [best available scientific knowledge and other relevant knowledge][best available scientific knowledge[ and][, including] information from diverse knowledge systems[,]] on ecological and biological features in marine areas beyond national jurisdiction in support of the potential development of future submissions, as appropriate and in accordance with the modalities contained in decision 16/16, without prejudicing future discussions of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice and the Conference of the Parties and in cooperation with [the Secretariat of the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction and] other competent international entities for the purpose of scientific and technical"},{"t":"7 The terms of reference for the Informal Advisory Group, which have been aligned with the modalities contained in the annex to"},{"t":"decision 16/16, are available at www.cbd.int/marine/ebsa/revised-tor-iag-on-ebsa.pdf."},{"t":"2/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"資源動員，以在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16，為《公約》下生態或生物重要海域之工作做出貢獻；","html":"<p>資源動員，以在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16，為《公約》下生態或生物重要海域之工作做出貢獻；</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"5.\n**進一步鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府及相關組織，在適當情況下並根據國家情況，利用最佳可用科學資訊與相容工具，並考慮識別與認定海洋物種之必要且特別敏感之棲息地，以支持生態或生物重要海域之描述與識別，並為以生態系為基礎之方法及區域性保育措施提供資訊，包括適當情況下海洋與沿海保護區及保育共生地之指定與管理，以支持《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 3，同時尊重相關國際法律文件與程序之授權；","html":"<p>5.<br />\n<strong>進一步鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府及相關組織，在適當情況下並根據國家情況，利用最佳可用科學資訊與相容工具，並考慮識別與認定海洋物種之必要且特別敏感之棲息地，以支持生態或生物重要海域之描述與識別，並為以生態系為基礎之方法及區域性保育措施提供資訊，包括適當情況下海洋與沿海保護區及保育共生地之指定與管理，以支持《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之目標 3，同時尊重相關國際法律文件與程序之授權；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"[6. **採納**關於符合生態或生物重要海域標準之區域描述之同儕審查程序之自願性[良好實務參考要素][指南]，如本決議附件一所載[及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準]，並**邀請**締約方、其他政府及主管之政府間組織在適當情況下並根據國家情況及主管政府間組織各自之授權與程序利用之，且不影響或修改根據其他程序所建立之同儕審查或決策程序，並**注意到**該自願性[參考要素][指南]不損害各國之主權、主權權利或管轄權；]","html":"<p>[6. <strong>採納</strong>關於符合生態或生物重要海域標準之區域描述之同儕審查程序之自願性[良好實務參考要素][指南]，如本決議附件一所載[及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準]，並<strong>邀請</strong>締約方、其他政府及主管之政府間組織在適當情況下並根據國家情況及主管政府間組織各自之授權與程序利用之，且不影響或修改根據其他程序所建立之同儕審查或決策程序，並<strong>注意到</strong>該自願性[參考要素][指南]不損害各國之主權、主權權利或管轄權；]</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"7.\n**請求**執行秘書按照其職權範圍⁷，繼續促進「生態或生物重要海域非正式諮詢小組」之工作，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前，於科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構會議上提交該工作之報告；","html":"<p>7.<br />\n<strong>請求</strong>執行秘書按照其職權範圍⁷，繼續促進「生態或生物重要海域非正式諮詢小組」之工作，並在第十八次締約方大會召開前，於科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構會議上提交該工作之報告；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"8.\n**亦請求**執行秘書將上述第 2 段所提之提交文件納入生態或生物重要海域之資料庫，並將其轉交聯合國大會，以期為其相關程序下之工作提供資訊，並同時轉交締約方、其他政府及相關國際組織；","html":"<p>8.<br />\n<strong>亦請求</strong>執行秘書將上述第 2 段所提之提交文件納入生態或生物重要海域之資料庫，並將其轉交聯合國大會，以期為其相關程序下之工作提供資訊，並同時轉交締約方、其他政府及相關國際組織；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"9.\n**進一步請求**執行秘書，在資源可用之情況下：","html":"<p>9.<br />\n<strong>進一步請求</strong>執行秘書，在資源可用之情況下：</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(a) 在適當情況下，包括與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支援中心合作，繼續促進並支持開發用於修改生態或生物重要海域描述及描述新區域之提交文件之工作，包括透過推廣、技術支援與能力建構；","html":"<p>(a) 在適當情況下，包括與區域及次區域技術與科學合作支援中心合作，繼續促進並支持開發用於修改生態或生物重要海域描述及描述新區域之提交文件之工作，包括透過推廣、技術支援與能力建構；</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"(b) 召開一場具有平衡區域代表性的全球專家工作坊，以彙整、綜合並審查關於國家管轄範圍外區域海洋生態與生物特徵之[最佳可用科學知識與其他相關知識][最佳可用科學知識[及][，包括]來自多元知識系統之[,]]資訊，以支持未來提交文件之潛在開發，在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16 所載之模式，且不損害科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構與締約方之未來討論，並與[《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定之秘書處]及其他主管國際實體合作，以進行科學與技術","html":"<p>(b) 召開一場具有平衡區域代表性的全球專家工作坊，以彙整、綜合並審查關於國家管轄範圍外區域海洋生態與生物特徵之[最佳可用科學知識與其他相關知識][最佳可用科學知識[及][，包括]來自多元知識系統之[,]]資訊，以支持未來提交文件之潛在開發，在適當情況下並根據決議 16/16 所載之模式，且不損害科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構與締約方之未來討論，並與[《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍外區域海洋生物多樣性保育及永續利用協定之秘書處]及其他主管國際實體合作，以進行科學與技術</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"---\n⁷ 非正式諮詢小組之職權範圍（已與決議 16/16 附件所載之模式一致）可於 www.cbd.int/marine/ebsa/revised-tor-iag-on-ebsa.pdf 取得。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁷ 非正式諮詢小組之職權範圍（已與決議 16/16 附件所載之模式一致）可於 www.cbd.int/marine/ebsa/revised-tor-iag-on-ebsa.pdf 取得。</p>","en":[8,9,10]}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p003.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"exchange, while ensuring complementarity and avoiding unnecessary duplication of or prejudicing work carried out under the Agreement, including with respect to area-based management tools; [(c) To compile experiences in the use of the information contained in the descriptions of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas, including in efforts to implement the KunmingMontreal Global Biodiversity Framework[, the Agreement on Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction] and other relevant international agreements and frameworks, and make that information available at a future meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice;]"},{"t":"II"},{"t":"Conservation and sustainable use of marine and coastal biodiversity"},{"t":"10. [Welcomes with appreciation][Takes note of] the entry into force on 17 January 2026 of the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction;"},{"t":"11. Expresses its appreciation to the Governments of Germany, Ireland, Norway and Sweden for their financial support for the convening of an expert workshop on scientific and technical work conducted under the Convention on Biological Diversity relevant to marine biodiversity in areas beyond national jurisdiction in Bergen, Norway, from 2 to 5 December 2025, and takes note of the outcomes of the workshop;"},{"t":"12. Encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant entities, including those in charge of regional sea conventions and action plans and regional fishery bodies, to strengthen coordination and cooperation at the global, regional and national levels on issues related to marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction, with [the participation of relevant stakeholders, including indigenous people and local communities, women and youth, among others][the participation of stakeholders][the full and effective participation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women, youth and other stakeholders];"},{"t":"13. Also encourages Parties, and invites other Governments and organizations with competence in areas beyond national jurisdiction, to use, as appropriate and in accordance with their respective mandates and jurisdictional scopes, the wide range of tools, guidance and experiences developed under the Convention in their work to conserve and sustainably use marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction, [such as in the implementation of the Agreement on Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction, ]including work to support capacitybuilding, scientific and technical cooperation and technology transfer, without prejudicing work carried out by those organizations and under relevant processes, while promoting synergies and avoiding the duplication of efforts;"},{"t":"14. Notes with concern the findings of the global report on collective progress in the implementation of the Framework that show that marine and coastal ecosystems consistently receive less attention than terrestrial ecosystems[and the fact that a significant greater proportion of reported protected areas and other effective area-based conservation measures in marine and coastal areas do not yet meet address the qualitative elements of Target 3 of the Framework, including effective conservation and management, ecological representativeness, connectivity and equitable governance];"},{"t":"15. Urges Parties, and invites other Governments and relevant organizations, to strengthen efforts to accelerate the implementation of the Framework in the context of marine and coastal ecosystems, including through enhanced policy coherence, scientific and technical cooperation, capacity-building, access to and transfer of technology and the mobilization of adequate financial resources from all sources;"},{"t":"3/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件 – 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"交換資訊，同時確保互補性，並避免不必要的重複或損害根據本公約所進行的工作，包括在區域性管理工具方面；\n[(c) 彙編使用生態或生物重要海域描述中所含資訊之經驗，包括在落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》[,《國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定》]及其他相關國際協議與綱要方面之努力，並在科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構未來的會議上提供該等資訊；]","html":"<p>交換資訊，同時確保互補性，並避免不必要的重複或損害根據本公約所進行的工作，包括在區域性管理工具方面；<br />\n[(c) 彙編使用生態或生物重要海域描述中所含資訊之經驗，包括在落實《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》[,《國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定》]及其他相關國際協議與綱要方面之努力，並在科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構未來的會議上提供該等資訊；]</p>","en":[1,2,3]},{"md":"II\n海洋與沿海生物多樣性的保育與永續利用","html":"<p>II<br />\n海洋與沿海生物多樣性的保育與永續利用</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"10. [表示歡迎並表示讚賞][注意到]《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於「國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定」已於 2026 年 1 月 17 日生效；\n11. 對德國、愛爾蘭、挪威及瑞典政府為召集於 2025 年 12 月 2 日至 5 日在挪威卑爾根舉行之專家工作坊提供財務支持表示感謝，該工作坊係針對在《生物多樣性公約》下進行且與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之科學與技術工作，並注意到該工作坊之成果；\n12. **鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府及相關實體，包括負責區域海域公約與行動計畫及區域漁業機構之實體，加強在全球、區域及國家層級針對國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關議題之協調與合作，並[包含相關利害關係人之參與，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年等][利害關係人之參與][原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人之充分且有效參與]；\n13. 亦**鼓勵**締約方，並**邀請**在國家管轄範圍以外區域具有權限之其他政府與組織，在不損害該等組織及根據相關程序所進行之工作之前提下，在落實國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用之工作中，視情況並根據其各自之職權與管轄範圍，使用在公約下開發之廣泛工具、指南與經驗，[例如在落實《國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定》方面，]包括支持能力建構、科學與技術合作及技術轉移之工作，同時促進協同效應並避免工作重複；\n14. **憂心地注意到**關於落實綱要集體進展之全球報告結果，該結果顯示海洋與沿海生態系所受到的關注持續低於陸域生態系[且在海洋與沿海區域所報告之保護區與保育共生地中，有顯著較大比例尚未符合或處理綱要目標 3 之品質要素，包括有效保育與管理、生態代表性、連結性及公平治理]；\n15. **敦促**締約方，並**邀請**其他政府與相關組織，在海洋與沿海生態系之背景下，加強加速落實綱要之努力，包括透過強化政策一致性、科學與技術合作、能力建構、技術取得與轉移，以及從所有來源動員充足之財務資源；","html":"<p>10. [表示歡迎並表示讚賞][注意到]《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於「國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定」已於 2026 年 1 月 17 日生效；<br />\n11. 對德國、愛爾蘭、挪威及瑞典政府為召集於 2025 年 12 月 2 日至 5 日在挪威卑爾根舉行之專家工作坊提供財務支持表示感謝，該工作坊係針對在《生物多樣性公約》下進行且與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之科學與技術工作，並注意到該工作坊之成果；<br />\n12. <strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府及相關實體，包括負責區域海域公約與行動計畫及區域漁業機構之實體，加強在全球、區域及國家層級針對國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關議題之協調與合作，並[包含相關利害關係人之參與，包括原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年等][利害關係人之參與][原住民族與地方社區、女性、青年及其他利害關係人之充分且有效參與]；<br />\n13. 亦<strong>鼓勵</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>在國家管轄範圍以外區域具有權限之其他政府與組織，在不損害該等組織及根據相關程序所進行之工作之前提下，在落實國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用之工作中，視情況並根據其各自之職權與管轄範圍，使用在公約下開發之廣泛工具、指南與經驗，[例如在落實《國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定》方面，]包括支持能力建構、科學與技術合作及技術轉移之工作，同時促進協同效應並避免工作重複；<br />\n14. <strong>憂心地注意到</strong>關於落實綱要集體進展之全球報告結果，該結果顯示海洋與沿海生態系所受到的關注持續低於陸域生態系[且在海洋與沿海區域所報告之保護區與保育共生地中，有顯著較大比例尚未符合或處理綱要目標 3 之品質要素，包括有效保育與管理、生態代表性、連結性及公平治理]；<br />\n15. <strong>敦促</strong>締約方，並<strong>邀請</strong>其他政府與相關組織，在海洋與沿海生態系之背景下，加強加速落實綱要之努力，包括透過強化政策一致性、科學與技術合作、能力建構、技術取得與轉移，以及從所有來源動員充足之財務資源；</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p004.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"[16. Decides to establish an informal advisory group on work conducted under the Convention in relation to marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction with the terms of reference provided in annex II to the present decision;"},{"t":"17. Requests the Informal Advisory Group on Work Conducted under the Convention on Biological Diversity in Relation to Marine Biodiversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction to provide a report on its progress for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;]"},{"t":"18. Requests the Executive Secretary, subject to the availability of resources:"},{"t":"(a) To cooperate further with the Division for Ocean Affairs and the Law of the Sea of the Office of Legal Affairs of the United Nations Secretariat and other entities with competence in marine areas beyond national jurisdiction, in particular with a view to sharing tools, guidance, expertise, experiences and best practices developed under the Convention relevant to marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction, as appropriate, within the mandates of the respective entities, in a manner that promotes coherence and coordination and without undermining, and with full respect for, relevant legal instruments and frameworks and the mandates and competence of global, regional, subregional and sectoral bodies;"},{"t":"[(b) To prepare updates to the following documents, taking into account the best available scientific knowledge and the traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities, with their free, prior and informed consent, 8 as appropriate and subject to the availability of resources, within the mandate and jurisdictional scope of the Convention, taking into account relevant work carried out under other international instruments, frameworks and competent global, regional, subregional and sectoral bodies, avoiding duplication and promoting complementarity and coherence, and to make them available for peer review by Parties and relevant organizations before providing them for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the nineteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties:"},{"t":"(i) The scientific guidance for selecting areas to establish a representative network of marine protected areas, including in open ocean waters and deep-sea habitats,9 taking into account knowledge gaps in various regions, maintaining a clear distinction between the scientific description of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and decisions concerning the identification, proposal, designation or establishment of marine protected areas or other area-based management tools by competent authorities and bodies, acknowledging ecological representativeness and connectivity as vital criteria for area-based conservation and recognizing and integrating diverse knowledge systems, including the traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities;"},{"t":"[(ii)"},{"t":"The voluntary specific workplan on biodiversity in cold-water areas within the jurisdictional scope of the Convention;10]"},{"t":"[(iii) The voluntary guidelines for the consideration of biodiversity in environmental impact assessments in marine and coastal areas and the draft guidance on biodiversity-inclusive strategic environmental assessment in marine and coastal areas;11]]"},{"t":"(c) To commission a report, to be prepared in collaboration with relevant organizations, on scientific and technical information on marine biological and ecological connectivity, including vertical connectivity, in particular in coastal, open-ocean and deep-sea ecosystems, in order to inform"},{"t":"8 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"9 Decision IX/20, annex II."},{"t":"10 Decision XIII/11, annex II."},{"t":"11 UNEP/CBD/COP/11/23, annex."},{"t":"4/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"[16. **決定**成立一非正式諮詢小組，負責處理《公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工作，其職權範圍如本決議附件 II 所載；\n17. **請求**「關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組」提交其進度報告，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議；]\n18. **請求**執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：","html":"<p>[16. <strong>決定</strong>成立一非正式諮詢小組，負責處理《公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工作，其職權範圍如本決議附件 II 所載；<br />\n17. <strong>請求</strong>「關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組」提交其進度報告，供科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構於第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議審議；]<br />\n18. <strong>請求</strong>執行秘書在資源可用的情況下：</p>","en":[1,2,3]},{"md":"(a) 於各相關實體之職權範圍內，視適當情況，與聯合國秘書處法律事務廳之海洋事務及海洋法司以及其他在國家管轄範圍以外海域具備權責之實體進一步合作，特別是為了分享在《公約》下開發、與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工具、指南、專業知識、經驗與最佳實務，其方式應促進一致性與協調，且不應損害並應充分尊重相關法律文書與框架，以及全球、區域、次區域及部門機構之職權與權責；","html":"<p>(a) 於各相關實體之職權範圍內，視適當情況，與聯合國秘書處法律事務廳之海洋事務及海洋法司以及其他在國家管轄範圍以外海域具備權責之實體進一步合作，特別是為了分享在《公約》下開發、與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工具、指南、專業知識、經驗與最佳實務，其方式應促進一致性與協調，且不應損害並應充分尊重相關法律文書與框架，以及全球、區域、次區域及部門機構之職權與權責；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"[(b) 在資源可用的情況下，於《公約》之職權與管轄範圍內，考量現有最佳科學知識以及在取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先及知情同意⁸之情況下，視適當情況，並考量其他國際文書、框架及具權責之全球、區域、次區域與部門機構所進行之相關工作，在避免重複並促進互補性與一致性的前提下，準備下列文件之更新版本，並在提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構於第十九次締約方大會召開前之會議審議前，提供予締約方及相關組織進行同儕審查：\n(i) 用於選擇建立具代表性海洋保護區網絡（包括大洋水域與深海棲息地）之科學指南，⁹ 應考量各區域之知識差距，並在生態或生物重要海洋區域之科學描述，與主管機關及機構進行海洋保護區或其他以區域為基礎之管理工具之識別、提議、指定或建立之決策之間，維持清晰之區分；承認生態代表性與連結性為區域保育之關鍵準則，並承認且整合多元知識系統，包括原住民族與地方社區之傳統知識；","html":"<p>[(b) 在資源可用的情況下，於《公約》之職權與管轄範圍內，考量現有最佳科學知識以及在取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先及知情同意⁸之情況下，視適當情況，並考量其他國際文書、框架及具權責之全球、區域、次區域與部門機構所進行之相關工作，在避免重複並促進互補性與一致性的前提下，準備下列文件之更新版本，並在提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構於第十九次締約方大會召開前之會議審議前，提供予締約方及相關組織進行同儕審查：<br />\n(i) 用於選擇建立具代表性海洋保護區網絡（包括大洋水域與深海棲息地）之科學指南，⁹ 應考量各區域之知識差距，並在生態或生物重要海洋區域之科學描述，與主管機關及機構進行海洋保護區或其他以區域為基礎之管理工具之識別、提議、指定或建立之決策之間，維持清晰之區分；承認生態代表性與連結性為區域保育之關鍵準則，並承認且整合多元知識系統，包括原住民族與地方社區之傳統知識；</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"[(ii) 關於《公約》管轄範圍內冷水域生物多樣性之自願性特定工作計畫；¹⁰]","html":"<p>[(ii) 關於《公約》管轄範圍內冷水域生物多樣性之自願性特定工作計畫；¹⁰]</p>","en":[7,8]},{"md":"[(iii) 關於在海洋與沿岸區域之環境影響評估中考量生物多樣性之自願性指南，以及關於在海洋與沿岸區域進行生物多樣性納入式策略性環境評估之指南草案；¹¹]]","html":"<p>[(iii) 關於在海洋與沿岸區域之環境影響評估中考量生物多樣性之自願性指南，以及關於在海洋與沿岸區域進行生物多樣性納入式策略性環境評估之指南草案；¹¹]]</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"(c) 委託與相關組織合作編製一份關於海洋生物與生態連結性（包括垂直連結性）之科學與技術資訊報告，特別是在沿岸、大洋與深海生態系中，以提供資訊","html":"<p>(c) 委託與相關組織合作編製一份關於海洋生物與生態連結性（包括垂直連結性）之科學與技術資訊報告，特別是在沿岸、大洋與深海生態系中，以提供資訊</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"---\n⁸「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。\n⁹ 決議 IX/20，附件 II。\n¹⁰ 決議 XIII/11，附件 II。\n¹¹ UNEP/CBD/COP/11/23，附件。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁸「自由、事先及知情同意」係指「事先及知情同意」、「自由、事先及知情同意」與「核准與參與」之三方術語。<br />\n⁹ 決議 IX/20，附件 II。<br />\n¹⁰ 決議 XIII/11，附件 II。<br />\n¹¹ UNEP/CBD/COP/11/23，附件。</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]},{"md":"4/10","html":"<p>4/10</p>","en":[16]}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p005.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"the implementation of the Framework, and make the report available for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(d) To develop, in collaboration with relevant organizations and experts, scientific guidance on the application of emerging technologies, including environmental DNA, remote sensing and other appropriate biodiversity monitoring tools, to support the assessment and monitoring of marine biodiversity, taking into account national circumstances, capacities and priorities, using the best available scientific information and considering methods of application that value the traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities, and accompany that guidance with an analysis of priorities and options for capacity-building and development for developing country Parties, in particular the least developed countries and small island developing States among them;"},{"t":"(e) To identify which of the gaps and areas in need of additional focus contained in the annex to decision 16/17 would benefit from the development of new guidance under the Convention to advance the implementation of the Framework with respect to marine and coastal biodiversity and island biodiversity for consideration by the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(f) To prepare an analysis on the status of the implementation of the programme of work on island biodiversity 12 in the context of the Framework, taking into consideration the disproportionate threats to island ecosystems, the inseparable links among marine, coastal and island ecosystems and the annex to decision 16/17, and to provide the analysis to the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice for its consideration at a meeting held before the nineteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties;"},{"t":"(g) To enhance further cooperation, collaboration or synergies, as appropriate, with the secretariats of other multilateral environmental agreements and global and regional organizations, in accordance with their respective mandates, including through the Sustainable Ocean Initiative global dialogue with regional sea organizations and regional fishery bodies, with regard to various thematic issues related to marine and coastal biodiversity and island biodiversity in support of the implementation of the Framework [and the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development13]."},{"t":"Annex I"},{"t":"Voluntary [reference elements for good practice][guidelines] on peer-review processes for the description of areas meeting the criteria for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas [and other relevant compatible and complementary scientific criteria]"},{"t":"I. Introduction"},{"t":"1. There are various processes, on a range of scales and in diverse contexts, for describing areas of significance in marine and coastal areas, including the scientific description and mapping of areas meeting the criteria for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas. The processes reflect a range of objectives, contexts and priorities and may be coordinated variously by intergovernmental or governmental entities, indigenous peoples and local communities, and non-governmental organizations. Some are focused on specific types of habitats, species or ecological processes, while others combine at least two of the above or have a broader scope. Processes other than those to describe ecologically or biologically significant marine areas may also be linked with management measures or used to inform related management decisions."},{"t":"12 Decision VIII/1, annex."},{"t":"13 General Assembly resolution 70/1."},{"t":"5/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 18(c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"綱要的實施，並將報告提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；","html":"<p>綱要的實施，並將報告提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(d) 與相關組織及專家合作，針對新興技術之應用制定科學指引，包括環境 DNA、遙測及其他適當的生物多樣性監測工具，以支持海洋生物多樣性的評估與監測，並考量各國國情、能力與優先事項，利用現有最佳科學資訊，並考慮能重視原住民族與地方社區傳統知識之應用方法；此外，該指引應隨附一份針對開發中國家締約方（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之能力建構與發展的優先事項及選項分析；","html":"<p>(d) 與相關組織及專家合作，針對新興技術之應用制定科學指引，包括環境 DNA、遙測及其他適當的生物多樣性監測工具，以支持海洋生物多樣性的評估與監測，並考量各國國情、能力與優先事項，利用現有最佳科學資訊，並考慮能重視原住民族與地方社區傳統知識之應用方法；此外，該指引應隨附一份針對開發中國家締約方（特別是其中的低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）之能力建構與發展的優先事項及選項分析；</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"(e) 識別決議 16/17 附件中所含之差距及需要額外關注之領域，其中哪些領域能透過在公約下制定新指引，以促進海洋、沿岸及島嶼生物多樣性綱要實施之進展，並提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；","html":"<p>(e) 識別決議 16/17 附件中所含之差距及需要額外關注之領域，其中哪些領域能透過在公約下制定新指引，以促進海洋、沿岸及島嶼生物多樣性綱要實施之進展，並提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十八次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(f) 在綱要脈絡下，針對島嶼生物多樣性工作計畫$^{12}$之實施現況進行分析，並考量島嶼生態系所面臨的不成比例威脅、海洋、沿岸與島嶼生態系之間不可分割的聯繫，以及決議 16/17 之附件，並將該分析提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十九次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；","html":"<p>(f) 在綱要脈絡下，針對島嶼生物多樣性工作計畫<sup>12</sup>之實施現況進行分析，並考量島嶼生態系所面臨的不成比例威脅、海洋、沿岸與島嶼生態系之間不可分割的聯繫，以及決議 16/17 之附件，並將該分析提交予科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構，供其在第十九次締約方大會召開前之會議進行審議；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(g) 視情況加強與其他多邊環境協議秘書處，以及全球與區域組織之進一步合作、協作或綜效，並依其各自之職權，包括透過「永續海洋倡議」與區域海域組織及區域漁業機構進行全球對話，針對與海洋、沿岸及島嶼生物多樣性相關之各種主題議題，以支持綱要之實施[以及 2030 年永續發展議程$^{13}$]。","html":"<p>(g) 視情況加強與其他多邊環境協議秘書處，以及全球與區域組織之進一步合作、協作或綜效，並依其各自之職權，包括透過「永續海洋倡議」與區域海域組織及區域漁業機構進行全球對話，針對與海洋、沿岸及島嶼生物多樣性相關之各種主題議題，以支持綱要之實施[以及 2030 年永續發展議程<sup>13</sup>]。</p>","en":[5,6]},{"md":"附件 I\n關於描述符合生態或生物重要海洋區域標準之領域[及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準]同儕審查程序之自願性[良好實務參考要素][指南]","html":"<p>附件 I<br />\n關於描述符合生態或生物重要海洋區域標準之領域[及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準]同儕審查程序之自願性[良好實務參考要素][指南]</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"I. 簡介","html":"<p>I. 簡介</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"1.\n目前存在多種在不同尺度與多元脈絡下，描述海洋與沿岸重要區域之程序，包括對符合生態或生物重要海洋區域標準之區域進行科學描述與製圖。這些程序反映了多樣化的目標、脈絡與優先事項，並可能由政府間或政府實體、原住民族與地方社區，以及非政府組織進行各種形式的協調。部分程序聚焦於特定類型的棲地、物種或生態過程，而其他程序則結合了上述至少兩者或具有更廣泛的範圍。除描述生態或生物重要海洋區域之程序外，其他程序亦可能與管理措施相連結，或用於為相關管理決策提供資訊。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n目前存在多種在不同尺度與多元脈絡下，描述海洋與沿岸重要區域之程序，包括對符合生態或生物重要海洋區域標準之區域進行科學描述與製圖。這些程序反映了多樣化的目標、脈絡與優先事項，並可能由政府間或政府實體、原住民族與地方社區，以及非政府組織進行各種形式的協調。部分程序聚焦於特定類型的棲地、物種或生態過程，而其他程序則結合了上述至少兩者或具有更廣泛的範圍。除描述生態或生物重要海洋區域之程序外，其他程序亦可能與管理措施相連結，或用於為相關管理決策提供資訊。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"---\n$^{12}$ 決議 VIII/1，附件。\n$^{13}$ 大會決議 70/1。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>12</sup> 決議 VIII/1，附件。<br />\n<sup>13</sup> 大會決議 70/1。</p>","en":[10,11,12]}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p006.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"2. In its decision 16/16, the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity14 emphasized that, in developing submissions for descriptions of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas or modifications to those descriptions, proponents should consider the need for a strong scientific basis with sufficient information, as well as the importance of transparency, which are common factors of such processes. In that regard, peer review is a vital factor contributing to the effectiveness of the processes. Peer review can take various forms but is intended to provide an opportunity for experts to evaluate information in order to strengthen its scientific basis and credibility, enhance process transparency and support the consistent application of agreed criteria."},{"t":"3. In the same decision, the Conference of the Parties requested the Executive Secretary to develop voluntary guidelines on peer-review processes for the description of areas meeting the criteria for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and other relevant compatible and complementary scientific criteria."},{"t":"II."},{"t":"Purpose"},{"t":"4. The present voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] are aimed at supporting, as appropriate, inclusive, effective, scientifically robust, equitable and transparent expert peer-review processes for the description of areas meeting the criteria for ecologically or biologically significant marine areas [and other relevant compatible and complementary scientific criteria]."},{"t":"5. The voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] are focused exclusively on expert peer reviews as a scientific and technical quality assurance mechanism. They are intended to strengthen the scientific basis of proposed descriptions and support the consistent application of agreed criteria, recognizing that the description of an area as meeting the criteria for an ecologically or biologically significant marine area does not, in itself, constitute the identification, designation or establishment of a marine protected area or other area-based management tool or prescribe any management measure."},{"t":"6. The voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] are non-prescriptive and flexible in nature and do not replace national peer-review and broader rights holder or stakeholder and other consultation processes. They are intended[, collectively or on an individual basis,] to serve as a reference for good practice in support of relevant decisions of the Conference of the Parties, in particular decision 16/16. While they are primarily intended to provide options to complement existing processes to those who are managing a peer-review process, they may also be useful for experts involved in peer reviews."},{"t":"7. Nothing in the present voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] shall prejudice work conducted under other international instruments, frameworks or competent organizations. Their use in such processes is voluntary and subject to the respective mandates, procedures and decisions pertaining to those instruments, frameworks or competent organizations."},{"t":"8. Nothing in the voluntary [reference elements][guidelines] gives rise to any changes to the modalities adopted in decision 16/16, nor any additional steps or requirements with respect to the process for the modification of descriptions of ecologically or biologically significant marine areas and the description of new areas under the Convention or any processes related to the application of relevant compatible and complementary scientific criteria."},{"t":"III."},{"t":"Voluntary [reference elements][guidelines]"},{"t":"A. Information regarding the criteria for which the area is being proposed"},{"t":"9. Sufficient information regarding the criteria against which the area is being proposed for assessment should be provided to those involved in the peer-review process and should include the following:"},{"t":"14 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"6/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"2.\n在其決議 16/16 中，生物多樣性公約締約方大會¹⁴ 強調，在編製生態或生物重要海域之描述或其描述之修訂提案時，提案者應考慮具備充足資訊之強大科學基礎之必要性，以及透明度之重要性，此兩者皆為此類程序之共同要素。就此而言，同儕審查是促進程序有效性之關鍵因素。同儕審查可採取多種形式，其目的在於提供專家評估資訊之機會，以強化其科學基礎與公信力、增進程序透明度，並支持一致性地應用已達成協議之標準。","html":"<p>2.<br />\n在其決議 16/16 中，生物多樣性公約締約方大會¹⁴ 強調，在編製生態或生物重要海域之描述或其描述之修訂提案時，提案者應考慮具備充足資訊之強大科學基礎之必要性，以及透明度之重要性，此兩者皆為此類程序之共同要素。就此而言，同儕審查是促進程序有效性之關鍵因素。同儕審查可採取多種形式，其目的在於提供專家評估資訊之機會，以強化其科學基礎與公信力、增進程序透明度，並支持一致性地應用已達成協議之標準。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"3.\n在同一決議中，締約方大會請求執行秘書針對符合生態或生物重要海域標準及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準之區域描述，制定關於同儕審查程序之自願性指南。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n在同一決議中，締約方大會請求執行秘書針對符合生態或生物重要海域標準及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準之區域描述，制定關於同儕審查程序之自願性指南。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"II.","html":"<p>II.</p>","pre":"，制定關於同儕審查程序之自願性指南。\n\n","en":[3,4]},{"md":"目的","html":"<p>目的</p>","pre":"同儕審查程序之自願性指南。\n\nII.\n\n","en":[5]},{"md":"4.\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 旨在適當地支持具包容性、有效性、科學穩健性、公平性且透明之專家同儕審查程序，以用於描述符合生態或生物重要海域標準 [及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準] 之區域。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 旨在適當地支持具包容性、有效性、科學穩健性、公平性且透明之專家同儕審查程序，以用於描述符合生態或生物重要海域標準 [及其他相關相容且互補之科學標準] 之區域。</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"5.\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 專注於將專家同儕審查作為一種科學與技術品質保證機制。其目的在於強化擬議描述之科學基礎，並支持一致性地應用已達成協議之標準；並承認將某一區域描述為符合生態或生物重要海域標準，其本身並不構成海洋保護區或其他以區域為基礎之管理工具之識別、指定或建立，亦不規定任何管理措施。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 專注於將專家同儕審查作為一種科學與技術品質保證機制。其目的在於強化擬議描述之科學基礎，並支持一致性地應用已達成協議之標準；並承認將某一區域描述為符合生態或生物重要海域標準，其本身並不構成海洋保護區或其他以區域為基礎之管理工具之識別、指定或建立，亦不規定任何管理措施。</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"6.\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 本質上不具強制性且具靈活性，並不取代國家級同儕審查以及更廣泛之權利持有者、利害關係人及其他諮詢程序。其目的 [無論是集體地或個別地] 是作為支持締約方大會相關決議（特別是決議 16/16）之良好實務參考。雖然其主要目的是為管理同儕審查程序之人員提供補充現有程序的選項，但對於參與同儕審查之專家亦可能有所幫助。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 本質上不具強制性且具靈活性，並不取代國家級同儕審查以及更廣泛之權利持有者、利害關係人及其他諮詢程序。其目的 [無論是集體地或個別地] 是作為支持締約方大會相關決議（特別是決議 16/16）之良好實務參考。雖然其主要目的是為管理同儕審查程序之人員提供補充現有程序的選項，但對於參與同儕審查之專家亦可能有所幫助。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"7.\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 之任何內容，均不應損害根據其他國際文書、框架或主管組織所進行之工作。於此類程序中使用本文件屬自願性質，且須受與該等文書、框架或主管組織相關之各自職權、程序及決議之約束。","html":"<p>7.<br />\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 之任何內容，均不應損害根據其他國際文書、框架或主管組織所進行之工作。於此類程序中使用本文件屬自願性質，且須受與該等文書、框架或主管組織相關之各自職權、程序及決議之約束。</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"8.\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 之任何內容，均不導致決議 16/16 所採納之模式發生任何變更，亦不涉及關於在公約下修訂生態或生物重要海域描述及描述新區域之程序，或關於應用相關相容且互補之科學標準之任何程序之任何額外步驟或要求。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n本自願性 [參考要素][指南] 之任何內容，均不導致決議 16/16 所採納之模式發生任何變更，亦不涉及關於在公約下修訂生態或生物重要海域描述及描述新區域之程序，或關於應用相關相容且互補之科學標準之任何程序之任何額外步驟或要求。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"III.","html":"<p>III.</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"自願性 [參考要素][指南]","html":"<p>自願性 [參考要素][指南]</p>","pre":"序之任何額外步驟或要求。\n\nIII.\n\n","en":[10,11]},{"md":"A.","html":"<p>A.</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"關於該區域所提議標準之資訊","html":"<p>關於該區域所提議標準之資訊</p>","en":[12]},{"md":"9.\n應向參與同儕審查程序之人員提供關於該區域所提議進行評估之標準之充足資訊，且應包括下列各項：","html":"<p>9.<br />\n應向參與同儕審查程序之人員提供關於該區域所提議進行評估之標準之充足資訊，且應包括下列各項：</p>","en":[13]},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />","en":[13]},{"md":"¹⁴ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。","html":"<p>¹⁴ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。</p>","en":[14,15]}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p007.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"(a) A full overview of the steps of the process for applying the criteria in question, including the steps that have been completed thus far;"},{"t":"(b) The nature of the criteria that are being applied (e.g. context or objectives) and all requirements, including any associated thresholds, that the area in question must meet;"},{"t":"B. (c) An indication of whether the area in question is associated with any other criteria;"},{"t":"(d) Information on any previous unsuccessful efforts to assess the area against the criteria."},{"t":"Clear justification of why the area meets the criteria"},{"t":"10. Given that the expert review process is focused on ensuring that the proposal is of a high quality, sufficient information should be provided to those involved in the review demonstrating that the area in question meets the criteria, including the following:"},{"t":"(a) A clear geographical delineation of the area, using appropriate formats, such as geographic information system files or geographical coordinates, and the rationale for the delineation;"},{"t":"(b) The geographical scope of the exercise or analysis that led to the proposal to describe the area in question as significant;"},{"t":"(c) An indication of whether the process that led to the proposal was limited to or specifically focused on certain types of features, habitats, species or ecosystem services;"},{"t":"(d) A clear explanation of the features of the area that contribute to the fulfilment of the relevant criteria, using the best available information and knowledge, including data or data-driven analyses, and, where appropriate, traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities;"},{"t":"(e) The gaps or uncertainties that may exist in the information or knowledge used, including a description of confidence levels, where appropriate, and an explanation of the ways in which the gaps are addressed, where applicable, such as through assumptions, extrapolation, modelling or the use of complementary knowledge sources, including an indication of the associated uncertainty to ensure scientific transparency and robustness;"},{"t":"(f) Full references or citations for all information and knowledge used, including statements on the availability or reproducibility of data, where needed;"},{"t":"(g) Applicable permissions for all information and knowledge used, including the best available science and traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities, with their free, prior and informed consent,15 consistent with national legislation and circumstances."},{"t":"C. Experts engaged in the peer-review process"},{"t":"11. The following factors should be borne in mind when engaging experts in the peer-review process:"},{"t":"(a) A sufficient number of appropriate experts in the topic under discussion should be engaged, under a clear rationale for their engagement, such as those from various rights holder and stakeholder groups, who would be participating in their expert capacity, giving due consideration to the participation of experts who were not involved in the development of the submission, including:"},{"t":"(i) Experts with scientific knowledge of the types of features, habitats, species or ecosystem services being discussed, ensuring that the peer-review group includes a sufficient number of experts with knowledge of all the main features of the area (e.g. two experts per area of expertise);"},{"t":"15 “Free, prior and informed consent” refers to the tripartite terminology of “prior and informed consent”, “free, prior and"},{"t":"informed consent” and “approval and involvement”."},{"t":"7/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(a) 針對所涉準則應用程序步驟的完整概述，包括迄今為止已完成的步驟；\n(b) 所應用準則之性質（例如：背景或目標），以及該所涉區域必須符合的所有要求，包括任何相關之門檻；","html":"<p>(a) 針對所涉準則應用程序步驟的完整概述，包括迄今為止已完成的步驟；<br />\n(b) 所應用準則之性質（例如：背景或目標），以及該所涉區域必須符合的所有要求，包括任何相關之門檻；</p>","en":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"md":"B.","html":"<p>B.</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(c) 指明該所涉區域是否與任何其他準則相關；","html":"<p>(c) 指明該所涉區域是否與任何其他準則相關；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(d) 針對先前曾嘗試根據準則評估該區域但未成功之努力，提供相關資訊。","html":"<p>(d) 針對先前曾嘗試根據準則評估該區域但未成功之努力，提供相關資訊。</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"對於該區域符合準則之明確理由","html":"<p>對於該區域符合準則之明確理由</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"10. 鑑於專家審查程序之重點在於確保提案具備高品質，應向參與審查之人員提供充足資訊，以證明該所涉區域符合準則，包括以下內容：\n(a) 該區域之清晰地理界線，使用適當格式（例如：地理資訊系統檔案或地理座標），以及界線劃定之理據；\n(b) 導致將該所涉區域描述為具重要性之作業或分析的地理範圍；\n(c) 指明導致該提案之程序是否僅限於或特別聚焦於特定類型的特徵、棲地、物種或生態系服務；\n(d) 使用現有最佳資訊與知識，清晰說明該區域有助於達成相關準則之特徵，包括資料或資料驅動之分析，並在適當時，納入原住民族與地方社區之傳統知識；\n(e) 所使用資訊或知識中可能存在之差距或不確定性，包括在適當時對信心水準之描述，以及在適用時對處理差距之方式進行說明（例如：透過假設、推論、建模或使用補充性知識來源），並指明相關之不確定性，以確保科學透明度與穩健性；\n(f) 所有所使用資訊與知識之完整參考文獻或引用，包括在必要時對資料可用性或可重複性之說明；\n(g) 所有所使用資訊與知識（包括現有最佳科學以及在符合國家立法與情況下，取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先與知情同意之傳統知識）之適用許可，¹⁵","html":"<p>10. 鑑於專家審查程序之重點在於確保提案具備高品質，應向參與審查之人員提供充足資訊，以證明該所涉區域符合準則，包括以下內容：<br />\n(a) 該區域之清晰地理界線，使用適當格式（例如：地理資訊系統檔案或地理座標），以及界線劃定之理據；<br />\n(b) 導致將該所涉區域描述為具重要性之作業或分析的地理範圍；<br />\n(c) 指明導致該提案之程序是否僅限於或特別聚焦於特定類型的特徵、棲地、物種或生態系服務；<br />\n(d) 使用現有最佳資訊與知識，清晰說明該區域有助於達成相關準則之特徵，包括資料或資料驅動之分析，並在適當時，納入原住民族與地方社區之傳統知識；<br />\n(e) 所使用資訊或知識中可能存在之差距或不確定性，包括在適當時對信心水準之描述，以及在適用時對處理差距之方式進行說明（例如：透過假設、推論、建模或使用補充性知識來源），並指明相關之不確定性，以確保科學透明度與穩健性；<br />\n(f) 所有所使用資訊與知識之完整參考文獻或引用，包括在必要時對資料可用性或可重複性之說明；<br />\n(g) 所有所使用資訊與知識（包括現有最佳科學以及在符合國家立法與情況下，取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先與知情同意之傳統知識）之適用許可，¹⁵</p>","en":[9,10,11,12,13]},{"md":"C.","html":"<p>C.</p>","en":[14]},{"md":"參與同儕審查程序之專家","html":"<p>參與同儕審查程序之專家</p>","pre":"之傳統知識）之適用許可，¹⁵\n\nC.\n\n","en":[14]},{"md":"11. 於參與同儕審查程序之專家時，應考慮以下因素：\n(a) 應聘請足夠數量且具備討論主題相關專業之專家，並具備明確的聘任理據（例如：來自不同權利持有者與利害關係人團體之專家），且該等專家將以專家身份參與，並應適當考慮聘請未參與提交文件編製之專家，包括：\n(i) 對所討論之特徵、棲地、物件或生態系服務類型具備科學知識之專家，確保同儕審查小組包含足夠數量具備該區域所有主要特徵知識之專家（例如：每個專業領域兩名專家）；","html":"<p>11. 於參與同儕審查程序之專家時，應考慮以下因素：<br />\n(a) 應聘請足夠數量且具備討論主題相關專業之專家，並具備明確的聘任理據（例如：來自不同權利持有者與利害關係人團體之專家），且該等專家將以專家身份參與，並應適當考慮聘請未參與提交文件編製之專家，包括：<br />\n(i) 對所討論之特徵、棲地、物件或生態系服務類型具備科學知識之專家，確保同儕審查小組包含足夠數量具備該區域所有主要特徵知識之專家（例如：每個專業領域兩名專家）；</p>","en":[15,16,17]},{"md":"---\n¹⁵「自由、事先與知情同意」係指「事先與知情同意」、「自由、事先與知情同意」及「核准與參與」之三方術語。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹⁵「自由、事先與知情同意」係指「事先與知情同意」、「自由、事先與知情同意」及「核准與參與」之三方術語。</p>","en":[18,19,20]}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p008.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"(ii) Experts in the methodological approaches used in the analysis;"},{"t":"(iii) Experts from indigenous peoples and local communities who have traditional knowledge relevant to the area in question;"},{"t":"(iv) Experts from various sectors and user groups, according to national circumstances and legislation;"},{"t":"(b) Experts should understand and disclose their actual or potential conflicts of interest, potentially using individual, signed, formal declarations, and their motivating factors for engaging in the process, and a consistent approach should be applied to the management of conflicts;"},{"t":"(c) A clear explanation should be provided of the types of input expected from the experts, which may vary depending on their area of expertise, and of the format of the expected final output of the process;"},{"t":"(d) Peer-review methods and timelines should be flexible to reflect the range of regional and institutional contexts, especially where data or resources are limited, without losing scientific reliability."},{"t":"D. Establishing and conducting the peer-review process"},{"t":"12. The timing of the implementation of a peer-review process should be chosen in such a way that the scientific foundation and quality of the process and of the information used can be ensured as effectively as possible. The process should be carefully crafted and conducted, considering the following features:"},{"t":"(a) Effective and equitable modalities, which may include a combination of approaches, that help to facilitate the robust review of the proposal;"},{"t":"(b) Clear steps and expected timelines that are consistently respected and clear explanations of any deviations;"},{"t":"(c) Clear rules of procedure and code of conduct that are set out, explained to everyone involved and consistently respected throughout the process, including rules for reporting in any public documentation discussions and information provided during the process, such as on the use of traditional knowledge of indigenous peoples and local communities, with their free, prior and informed consent, consistent with national legislation and circumstances;"},{"t":"(d) Clear plans for the consideration of input received through the process and, where appropriate, for its incorporation and reflection in the output of the process, recognizing that not all input can be incorporated;"},{"t":"(e) Information on the ways in which the peer-review process influenced the final proposal, including a clear justification for any expert input that is not incorporated into the final output, as well as any dissenting views regarding the final output, in order to ensure transparency and the scientific reliability of the outcome;"},{"t":"(f) Adherence to any rules, procedures, timelines and expectations articulated at the outset of the process;"},{"t":"(g) Public availability of the outputs of the process, as well as input received during the process, as appropriate;"},{"t":"8/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程項目 18 (c) 之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0,1,2]},{"md":"(ii)","html":"<p>(ii)</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"用於分析之方法論路徑之專家；","html":"<p>用於分析之方法論路徑之專家；</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"(iii)","html":"<p>(iii)</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"擁有與所涉領域相關傳統知識之原住民族與地方社區專家；","html":"<p>擁有與所涉領域相關傳統知識之原住民族與地方社區專家；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(iv)","html":"<p>(iv)</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"根據國家情況與立法所選定之來自各領域與使用者群體之專家；","html":"<p>根據國家情況與立法所選定之來自各領域與使用者群體之專家；</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"(b) 專家應理解並揭露其實際或潛在之利益衝突，可透過個人簽署之正式聲明方式進行，並應說明其參與此程序之動機，且衝突管理應採取一致之方法；\n(c) 應針對預期從專家處獲得之投入類型（其可能因專業領域而異）以及此程序預期最終產出之格式，提供清晰之說明；\n(d) 同儕審查之方法與時程應具靈活性，以反映各種區域與制度背景，特別是在資料或資源有限之情況下，且不應喪失科學可靠性。","html":"<p>(b) 專家應理解並揭露其實際或潛在之利益衝突，可透過個人簽署之正式聲明方式進行，並應說明其參與此程序之動機，且衝突管理應採取一致之方法；<br />\n(c) 應針對預期從專家處獲得之投入類型（其可能因專業領域而異）以及此程序預期最終產出之格式，提供清晰之說明；<br />\n(d) 同儕審查之方法與時程應具靈活性，以反映各種區域與制度背景，特別是在資料或資源有限之情況下，且不應喪失科學可靠性。</p>","en":[5,6,7,8,9]},{"md":"D.","html":"<p>D.</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"建立與執行同儕審查程序","html":"<p>建立與執行同儕審查程序</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"12. 同儕審查程序執行之時機，其選擇應能確保此程序之科學基礎與品質，以及所使用資訊之品質，並盡可能有效；此程序之制定與執行應審慎，並考量下列特徵：\n(a) 有效且公平之模式，其中可包含多種方法之結合，以協助促進對提案之穩健審查；\n(b) 應一貫遵守之清晰步驟與預期時程，以及對任何偏差之清晰說明；\n(c) 應制定清晰之程序規則與行為準則，並向所有參與者進行說明，且在整個程序中應一貫遵守，包括在任何公開文件討論中進行報告之規則，以及程序期間所提供之資訊，例如關於在符合國家立法與情況下，取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先及知情同意後使用其傳統知識之規定；\n(d) 應針對考量透過此程序所獲得之投入，以及在適當情況下將其納入並反映於此程序產出之做法，制定清晰之計畫，並承認並非所有投入皆能被納入；\n(e) 應提供關於同儕審查程序如何影響最終提案之資訊，包括對於任何未納入最終產出之專家投入提供清晰之理由，以及對於最終產出之任何異議，以確保結果之透明度與科學可靠性；\n(f) 應遵守於程序開始時所闡明之任何規則、程序、時程與預期；\n(g) 在適當情況下，應使此程序之產出以及程序期間所獲得之投入可供大眾取得；","html":"<p>12. 同儕審查程序執行之時機，其選擇應能確保此程序之科學基礎與品質，以及所使用資訊之品質，並盡可能有效；此程序之制定與執行應審慎，並考量下列特徵：<br />\n(a) 有效且公平之模式，其中可包含多種方法之結合，以協助促進對提案之穩健審查；<br />\n(b) 應一貫遵守之清晰步驟與預期時程，以及對任何偏差之清晰說明；<br />\n(c) 應制定清晰之程序規則與行為準則，並向所有參與者進行說明，且在整個程序中應一貫遵守，包括在任何公開文件討論中進行報告之規則，以及程序期間所提供之資訊，例如關於在符合國家立法與情況下，取得原住民族與地方社區之自由、事先及知情同意後使用其傳統知識之規定；<br />\n(d) 應針對考量透過此程序所獲得之投入，以及在適當情況下將其納入並反映於此程序產出之做法，制定清晰之計畫，並承認並非所有投入皆能被納入；<br />\n(e) 應提供關於同儕審查程序如何影響最終提案之資訊，包括對於任何未納入最終產出之專家投入提供清晰之理由，以及對於最終產出之任何異議，以確保結果之透明度與科學可靠性；<br />\n(f) 應遵守於程序開始時所闡明之任何規則、程序、時程與預期；<br />\n(g) 在適當情況下，應使此程序之產出以及程序期間所獲得之投入可供大眾取得；</p>","en":[11,12,13,14,15]},{"md":"8/10","html":"<p>8/10</p>","en":[16]}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p009.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"(h) Provisions for the adaptive improvement of the peer-review process for future exercises."},{"t":"[Annex II"},{"t":"Terms of reference for the Informal Advisory Group on Work Conducted under the Convention on Biological Diversity in Relation to Marine Biodiversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction"},{"t":"1. The Informal Advisory Group on Work Conducted under the Convention on Biological Diversity16 in relation to Marine Biodiversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction shall respect and take fully into account the mandates and work of other competent entities and intergovernmental organizations with respect to the conservation and sustainable use of marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction, as well as previous guidance given by the Conference of the Parties to the Convention regarding the role of the Convention in that context, and shall conduct its work in a manner that promotes coherence and coordination."},{"t":"2. The Informal Advisory Group shall:"},{"t":"(a) Provide scientific and technical advice to the Secretariat of the Convention on work relevant to marine biodiversity in areas beyond national jurisdiction, in particular on the prioritization of and approaches for possible activities and initiatives, within the mandate and jurisdictional scope of the Convention, drawing on opportunities identified during the expert workshop on scientific and technical work conducted under the Convention relevant to marine biodiversity in areas beyond national jurisdiction held in Bergen, Norway, from 2 to 5 December 2025;17"},{"t":"[(b) Identify timely opportunities for specific areas of cooperation, collaboration or synergies, as appropriate, with the Secretariat of the Agreement under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea on the Conservation and Sustainable Use of Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction18 and other competent entities and international organizations with respect to the conservation and sustainable use of marine biodiversity of areas beyond national jurisdiction, including opportunities for the Conference of the Parties to the Convention and the subsidiary bodies to contribute relevant scientific and technical information, drawing on cooperation opportunities identified at the expert workshop noted above;"},{"t":"(c) Provide advice on areas of potential cooperation, collaboration or synergies, as appropriate and in line with the mandate and jurisdictional scope of the Convention, on relevant scientific and technical information to inform work under the Agreement on Marine Biological Diversity of Areas beyond National Jurisdiction.]"},{"t":"3. The Informal Advisory Group shall be composed of up to 20 experts nominated by Parties, with equal representation of the five regional groups, up to 10 experts nominated by intergovernmental bodies with competence in the conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity of marine areas beyond national jurisdiction, and up to 7 experts nominated by other relevant organizations[, including from civil society and indigenous peoples and local communities]. The Executive Secretary, in consultation with the Bureau of the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice, shall select experts from the nominees with due regard to a diversity of relevant technical expertise, geographical representation, including from least developed countries and small island developing States, gender balance [and the representation of indigenous peoples and local communities, women’s and youth groups, and relevant stakeholders]."},{"t":"4. The Informal Advisory Group is established for a two-year period [that may be renewed by a decision of the Conference of the Parties]. The members of the Group shall be selected for a twoyear period. The work of the Group should continue regardless of any changes in membership."},{"t":"16 United Nations, Treaty Series, vol. 1760, No. 30619."},{"t":"17 See CBD/MCB/WS/2025/1/2."},{"t":"18 A/CONF.232/2023/4."},{"t":"9/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0,1]},{"md":"(h)","html":"<p>(h)</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"針對未來作業建立同儕審查程序適應性改進之規定。","html":"<p>針對未來作業建立同儕審查程序適應性改進之規定。</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"[附件 II\n關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組職權範圍","html":"<p>[附件 II<br />\n關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組職權範圍</p>","en":[3]},{"md":"1.\n關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組¹⁶，應尊重並充分考慮其他具職能之實體與政府間組織在國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面之職權與工作，以及締約方大會先前就該公約在此脈絡下之角色所提供之指引，並應以促進一致性與協調之方式開展其工作。","html":"<p>1.<br />\n關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關工作之非正式諮詢小組¹⁶，應尊重並充分考慮其他具職能之實體與政府間組織在國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面之職權與工作，以及締約方大會先前就該公約在此脈絡下之角色所提供之指引，並應以促進一致性與協調之方式開展其工作。</p>","en":[4]},{"md":"2.\n該非正式諮詢小組應：","html":"<p>2.<br />\n該非正式諮詢小組應：</p>","en":[5]},{"md":"(a) 在《生物多樣性公約》之職權與管轄範圍內，針對與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工作，特別是關於可能活動與倡議之優先順序及方法，向本公約秘書處提供科學與技術建議，並利用 2025 年 12 月 2 日至 5 日於挪威卑爾根舉行之關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之科學與技術工作專家工作坊中所識別之機會；¹⁷","html":"<p>(a) 在《生物多樣性公約》之職權與管轄範圍內，針對與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之工作，特別是關於可能活動與倡議之優先順序及方法，向本公約秘書處提供科學與技術建議，並利用 2025 年 12 月 2 日至 5 日於挪威卑爾根舉行之關於《生物多樣性公約》下與國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性相關之科學與技術工作專家工作坊中所識別之機會；¹⁷</p>","en":[6]},{"md":"[(b) 在適當情況下，針對特定合作、協作或綜效領域，與《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定¹⁸之秘書處，以及其他在國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面具職能之實體與國際組織，識別及時之合作機會，包括締約方大會與附屬機構提供相關科學與技術資訊之機會，並利用上述所提及之專家工作坊中所識別之合作機會；","html":"<p>[(b) 在適當情況下，針對特定合作、協作或綜效領域，與《聯合國海洋法公約》下關於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用協定¹⁸之秘書處，以及其他在國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面具職能之實體與國際組織，識別及時之合作機會，包括締約方大會與附屬機構提供相關科學與技術資訊之機會，並利用上述所提及之專家工作坊中所識別之合作機會；</p>","en":[7]},{"md":"(c) 在適當情況下且符合本公約之職權與管轄範圍內，針對潛在合作、協作或綜效領域，就相關科學與技術資訊提供建議，以利於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定下之工作。]","html":"<p>(c) 在適當情況下且符合本公約之職權與管轄範圍內，針對潛在合作、協作或綜效領域，就相關科學與技術資訊提供建議，以利於國家管轄範圍以外區域海洋生物多樣性協定下之工作。]</p>","en":[8]},{"md":"3.\n該非正式諮詢小組應由締約方提名之不超過 20 名專家組成，且五個區域組應具備平等代表性；由在國家管轄範圍以外海洋區域生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面具職能之政府間機構提名之不超過 10 名專家；以及由其他相關組織提名之不超過 7 名專家[, 包括來自公民社會、原住民族與地方社區之專家]。執行秘書應在諮詢科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構局後，從提名人中選出專家，並應適當考慮相關技術專業之多樣性、地理代表性（包括來自低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、性別平衡 [以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年團體及相關利害關係人之代表性]。","html":"<p>3.<br />\n該非正式諮詢小組應由締約方提名之不超過 20 名專家組成，且五個區域組應具備平等代表性；由在國家管轄範圍以外海洋區域生物多樣性保育與永續利用方面具職能之政府間機構提名之不超過 10 名專家；以及由其他相關組織提名之不超過 7 名專家[, 包括來自公民社會、原住民族與地方社區之專家]。執行秘書應在諮詢科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構局後，從提名人中選出專家，並應適當考慮相關技術專業之多樣性、地理代表性（包括來自低度開發國家與小島嶼開發中國家）、性別平衡 [以及原住民族與地方社區、女性與青年團體及相關利害關係人之代表性]。</p>","en":[9]},{"md":"4.\n該非正式諮詢小組之設立期限為兩年 [此期限可經締約方大會決議予以展延]。小組成員之任期應為兩年。無論成員是否變動，小組之工作應持續進行。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n該非正式諮詢小組之設立期限為兩年 [此期限可經締約方大會決議予以展延]。小組成員之任期應為兩年。無論成員是否變動，小組之工作應持續進行。</p>","en":[10]},{"md":"¹⁶ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。\n¹⁷ 參閱 CBD/MCB/WS/2025/1/2。\n¹⁸ A/CONF.232/2023/4。","html":"<p>¹⁶ 聯合國，條約集，第 1760 卷，第 30619 號。<br />\n¹⁷ 參閱 CBD/MCB/WS/2025/1/2。<br />\n¹⁸ A/CONF.232/2023/4。</p>","en":[11,12,13]},{"md":"9/10","html":"<p>9/10</p>","en":[14]}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ad7132045af13551e4861f5/p010.md","en":[{"t":"Non-paper on item 18 (c) – version 2 – 20 October 2026"},{"t":"5. The Informal Advisory Group may invite experts from outside the Group, as appropriate[, including experts and representatives of indigenous peoples and local communities, women and youth,] to contribute to discussions on specific issues considered by the Group."},{"t":"6. The Informal Advisory Group will primarily conduct its work online and, subject to the availability of resources, will also meet in person."},{"t":"7. The Informal Advisory Group is to start its work immediately after the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties and report on its work to the Subsidiary Body on Scientific, Technical and Technological Advice at a meeting held before the eighteenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties.]"},{"t":"__________"},{"t":"10/10"}],"blocks":[{"md":"關於議程第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日","html":"<p>關於議程第 18 (c) 項之非正式文件（Non-paper）– 第 2 版 – 2026 年 10 月 20 日</p>","en":[0]},{"md":"5.\n非正式諮詢小組得視情況**邀請**小組外部之專家，[包括原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的專家與代表]，以對小組所考量之特定議題討論做出貢獻。","html":"<p>5.<br />\n非正式諮詢小組得視情況<strong>邀請</strong>小組外部之專家，[包括原住民族與地方社區、女性及青年的專家與代表]，以對小組所考量之特定議題討論做出貢獻。</p>","en":[1]},{"md":"6.\n非正式諮詢小組將主要透過線上方式進行工作，且在資源可用的情況下，亦將進行實體會議。","html":"<p>6.<br />\n非正式諮詢小組將主要透過線上方式進行工作，且在資源可用的情況下，亦將進行實體會議。</p>","en":[2]},{"md":"7.\n非正式諮詢小組應於第十七屆締約方大會召開後立即開始其工作，並於第十八屆締約方大會召開前之會議上，向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告其工作成果。]","html":"<p>7.<br />\n非正式諮詢小組應於第十七屆締約方大會召開後立即開始其工作，並於第十八屆締約方大會召開前之會議上，向科學、技術及工藝諮詢附屬機構報告其工作成果。]</p>","en":[3,4,5]}]}]};
